examples/figure13/llama_output_old_hallucinated.json

# Vocab-scan large outputs (multi-100s of MB to 1+ GiB). Kept locally
# for re-analysis but never committed; the small `*_phonological_clean.json`
# subset is committed for the rebuttal record.
docs/experiments/**/vocab_scan_*_raw.json
docs/experiments/**/vocab_scan_*_phonological.json
!docs/experiments/**/vocab_scan_*_phonological_clean.json

# Figure-13 newline census: the dense JumpReLU (Qwen) census JSONs are 53-237 MB
# each (all active features x all positions x decoder-top lists). Kept locally
# for re-analysis; the small mntss (Gemma/Llama) census, all fullline_*.json,
# and findings.md are committed. Regenerate via `figure13_newline_census`.
docs/experiments/figure13-newline/census_qwen3-*.json

# Maar replication: keep prompts JSONs committed (small, audit-relevant);
# ignore the downloaded supplementary .zip (large, license-uncertain) and
# the extracted supplementary tree (60 MB of Maar's code; redownload via
# scripts/maar_supplementary_fetch.py if needed).
!examples/results/maar_contrastive_steering/prompts/*.json
examples/results/maar_contrastive_steering/*.zip
examples/results/maar_contrastive_steering/maar_supp/
